  "scope": "Finite cutoff and fixed positive floor for the hash-pinned L=16 A1 six-real production model; common real-even mutually orthogonal one-shot sharp shells; bounded cylindrical strict-past controls, or sufficiently integrable regular controls for which every displayed product is finite. A general progressive flow that revisits a Fourier range and extension to arbitrary finite-energy drifts are excluded.",
  "theorem": {
    "full_score": "F_j(u)=I_j(u)+C_j(u)=V_j^ren(Z_<j+K_j u)-V_(j-1)^ren(Z_<j), so s_j=ell_j+m_j is the full shell-energy gradient.",
    "square_coupled_charge": "E_j F_j(xi_j+h)=-|h|^2/(2q)-S_j^sharp(h), with S_j^sharp=q<s_j,R_j s_j>/2-E_j N_j(xi_j+h)-|H_j^(1/2)(h+qR_j s_j)|^2/2.",
    "gibbs_pythagoras": "S_j^sharp(h)=kappa_j-q^(-1)H(gamma_h|nu_j), with the state-past pullback required in the triangular entropy chain.",
    "backward_heat_martingale": "B_j^(J)=P_(Sigma_(j+1:J))B and W_j^(J)=B_j^(J):(Dstate^2-Gamma_j)/2 satisfy E_j W_j^(J)(x+g_j,y+d_j)=W_(j-1)^(J)(x,y), yielding the exact controlled telescope.",
    "quartic_carrier": "For f(A)=cA^4, the ell+m score, nonlinear remainder, and retained square exactly reassemble the factor-four carrier; charge-alone and terminal-only shell estimates are invalid.",
    "averaged_frame_secant": "Heat averaging preserves the PSD frame and the exact four-term Cartan secant, including the positive Gauss-Newton square.",
    "closed_reduction": "For every zeta,eta>0 and a fixed sufficiently large j0, E V_J^ren(Z_J)>=-zeta E||Z_J||_6^6-eta E sum_j||h_j||^2-C+E sum_(j>=j0) R_j uniformly in J within the regular control class.",
    "remaining_form": "R_j is the averaged raw-current secant w^T Q Delta w+(Delta w)^T Q Delta w/2. Its cutoff-uniform lower bound is the sole remaining analytic form theorem within the regular one-shot class."
  },
